# === Local AI tooling ===
# .harness/ holds the local AI agent harness (hooks, agents, rules, skills,
# workflows). The tool directories below are symlinks into .harness/ plus
# generated per-tool config and personal permission settings
# (e.g. .claude/settings.local.json). None of this is part of the package
# and it must not be published.
.harness/
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/
.agent/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
paseo.json

# === Python build, packaging, caches ===
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
*.so
*.o
*.a
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
# MkDocs build output (mkdocs.yml has no explicit site_dir, so `mkdocs build`
# writes to ./site/). The built site is a generated artifact; the sources live
# in docs_site/.
site/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# === Virtual environments ===
.venv/
venv/
env/

# === Editor / OS noise ===
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# === Generated artifacts (see .harness/rules/common/scope.md) ===
# Computation/verification outputs (CSV / PNG / result JSON / large binaries)
# are never committed. Intentional figures or reference data under docs/ and
# tests/ are re-included by the negation patterns below.
*.csv
*.png
result*.json
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.csv
# Documentation-site assets. The blanket *.csv / *.png excludes above were
# written when docs/ was the only documentation tree, so their re-inclusions
# only cover docs/**. Without the line below, a diagram or reference dataset
# placed under docs_site/docs/assets/ is silently never committed: the local
# build stays green, the CI clean checkout has no such file, and MkDocs does
# not treat a missing image as an error -- so CI stays green too and the
# local documentation site simply loses the figure. Keep source assets visible
# to a clean checkout.
!docs_site/docs/assets/**
!tests/**/*.csv
!tests/**/*.npy
!tests/**/*.npz
!tests/**/*.h5
!tests/**/*.hdf5

# === References / Large Binaries ===
*.pdf
*.zip
